Sounds to me like you are a Lojbanologist rather than a Lojbbanist.  Barrin=
g someone actually writing a good text book (on the record, a low probabili=
ty event) learning Lojban has always been a massive memory project with lot=
s of writing, making mistakes, arguing about corrections and then going bac=
k at it again.  Learning *about* Lojban, however, is pretty straightforward=
 and can be done quite a bit by reading CLL and various bits from these lis=
ts. Have at it!
As for your own conlangs, I would take them to the Conlangers group on Face=
book, which is friendly and helpful.


